  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only setup so far is multiprofile + scvi_n200 + transformer (config_006, acc=0.653), and scvi_n200 consistently outperforms pca_n2000 across both profile settings. However, scgpt is entirely untested, leaving a critical uncertainty about whether a third encoder could substantially improve the RNA signal before we commit budget to multimodal fusion experiments. Question: Does scgpt match or exceed scvi_n200 under the same multiprofile + transformer conditions? This is a clean 1-factor comparison (encoder) against config_006. Why this is the best next step: The RNA encoder is the most fundamental design choice—it determines the quality of the primary signal in every downstream multimodal experiment. Resolving whether scgpt is competitive (or superior) before testing multimodal fusion avoids wasting limited budget on multimodal configs built on a suboptimal encoder. If scgpt ≈ scvi_n200, we confirm the current best and pivot to multimodal; if scgpt is markedly better, we redirect the multimodal search toward scgpt-based configs."
}

